---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SiteSearch from '~/components/common/SiteSearch.astro';
import { getBlogPermalink } from '~/utils/permalinks';

const metadata = {
  title: 'CodeRiff - Independent software engineering',
  description: 'Based in Málaga. Working worldwide.',
};
---

<PageLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pb-24 pt-24 sm:pt-36 lg:px-8">
    <p class="mb-6 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">Independent software engineering</p>
    <h1 class="max-w-4xl text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-heading sm:text-7xl">
      Software engineering, built on <span class="text-primary">experience</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
      More than 20 years designing, building and evolving software systems, from Málaga to the world.
    </p>
    <SiteSearch />
    <a
      class="mt-8 inline-block text-base font-semibold text-primary underline decoration-primary/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary"
      href="#services">Explore what we do <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a
    >
  </section>

  <section
    id="services"
    class="scroll-mt-20 border-y border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 py-20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/40"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">Services</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading sm:text-4xl">
        From an idea to software that works.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article>
          <span class="text-sm text-muted">01</span><h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-heading">
            .NET development
          </h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
            Deep experience with C# and .NET, building modern applications, APIs, services and information systems
            designed to evolve with the business.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="text-sm text-muted">02</span><h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-heading">
            Architecture & distributed systems
          </h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
            Practical experience designing systems using Event Sourcing, CQRS and event-driven architectures, as well as
            APIs, messaging and system integrations. Architecture driven by the problem.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="text-sm text-muted">03</span><h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-heading">
            Software engineering & consultancy
          </h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
            More than two decades of hands-on software engineering experience, from designing new systems to modernising
            existing ones, solving difficult technical problems and helping teams make better engineering decisions.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="scroll-mt-20 mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] md:gap-16">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">About</p>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading sm:text-4xl">
          More than 20 years building software.
        </h2><p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
          CodeRiff is an independent software engineering endeavour based in Málaga, Spain, backed by more than two
          decades of experience developing and engineering software.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
          We specialise in the .NET ecosystem and information systems, with particular experience in Event Sourcing,
          CQRS and event-driven architectures.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
          We believe good engineering starts with understanding the problem. Technology, architecture and patterns come
          afterwards.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
          The goal is software that solves the right problem, is understandable by the people working with it, and can
          continue evolving for years to come Based in the Costa del Sol. Remote by design. Working worldwide.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="blog"
    class="scroll-mt-20 border-y border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 py-20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/40"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">From the blog</p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col justify-between gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-end">
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading sm:text-4xl">Notes on making the web better.</h2><p
            class="mt-4 text-muted dark:text-slate-300"
          >
            Ideas, lessons and useful things we learn along the way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-primary underline decoration-primary/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary"
          href={getBlogPermalink()}>Visit the blog <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
      </div>
      <article class="mt-10 border-t border-gray-200 pt-6 dark:border-slate-700">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-primary">A note on software design</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-heading">
          <a class="hover:text-primary" href="/blog/problem-first-software-design"
            >Understand the problem before designing the solution</a
          >
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
          Event Storming, strategic DDD, and vertical slices help teams build a shared model before AI makes it easier
          to build the wrong thing faster.
        </p>
        <a
          class="mt-4 inline-flex font-semibold text-primary hover:underline"
          href="/blog/problem-first-software-design">Read the article <span class="ml-2" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-20 mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-8">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">Contact</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading sm:text-4xl">Let's build something.</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
      Have an idea, an existing system that needs attention, or an engineering challenge you'd like to discuss?
    </p>
    <form
      id="contact-form"
      method="POST"
      action={`https://formsubmit.co/${import.meta.env.PUBLIC_FORMSUBMIT_TOKEN ?? ''}`}
      class="mt-8 grid max-w-xl gap-4"
    >
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="New CodeRiff website enquiry" />
      <input type="hidden" name="_template" value="table" />
      <input type="hidden" name="_next" value="https://coderiff.net/?contact=sent#contact" />
      <input type="hidden" name="_url" value="https://coderiff.net/" />
      <input type="text" name="_honey" class="hidden" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />
      <label class="grid gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-heading" for="contact-name">
        Full name
        <input
          id="contact-name"
          name="name"
          type="text"
          required
          maxlength="160"
          autocomplete="name"
          class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 font-normal dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-slate-900"
        />
      </label>
      <label class="grid gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-heading" for="contact-email">
        Email
        <input
          id="contact-email"
          name="email"
          type="email"
          required
          maxlength="254"
          autocomplete="email"
          class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 font-normal dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-slate-900"
        />
      </label>
      <label class="grid gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-heading" for="contact-message">
        How can I help?
        <textarea
          id="contact-message"
          name="message"
          required
          maxlength="5000"
          rows="5"
          class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 font-normal dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-slate-900"
        ></textarea>
      </label>
      <button type="submit" class="btn-primary w-fit">Send message</button>
    </form>
    <script>
      if (new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('contact') === 'sent') {
        const form = document.querySelector('#contact-form');
        if (form) {
          form.hidden = true;
          form.insertAdjacentHTML(
            'beforebegin',
            '<p class="mt-6 text-lg font-medium text-primary" role="status">Thanks, your message has been sent.</p>'
          );
        }
      }
    </script>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
